# The scalars and one bit of the data bus are pinned; the rest of the
# address and data buses are left to the placer, which is legal: Reticle
# checks what is stated, not that everything is stated.
#
# rdata[0] was on pin 99 until 2026-09-24, when a bus constrained bit by
# bit first had its bits' pins honoured (before that, this line pinned
# nothing). On the synthetic iCE40 fabric pins 97, 98 and 99 then do not
# route: one local track near X10Y1 stays wanted by two signals however
# many iterations the router gets. Every other free pin routes, so the
# bit is on 95; the corner is a limit of the fabric model and the router,
# recorded here rather than worked around silently.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 clk 21
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 we 8
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 rdata[0] 95
create_clock -name sys -period 83.333 clk
region core 1 1 6 6
assign rd region core
keep_hierarchy wr
set_multicycle_path 2 -from waddr -to rdata
